## Every deviation goes in DEVIATIONS.md

If you do anything the paper's stated protocol doesn't call for (a normalization it doesn't
mention, a default hyperparameter substituted for one the paper specifies, a workaround for a
build issue), write it to `{{ output_dir }}/DEVIATIONS.md` as you go. An empty DEVIATIONS.md is
only legal if you explicitly assert "no divergences found" -- don't leave it silently blank.

Do not try to make the numbers match the paper by adjusting the model. Scientific fidelity to what
the paper's method actually does, cited and logged, is the goal -- not agreement with a reported
number.

